<<~ ahu slot=`#/meme-header`>>

! Lararium Signal Docs

Not invariant law.
This shelf holds the lararium-side signal frame that binds agent and operator.
The l-space definition, HUD, drift, provenance, and render-target documents live below this loci.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/room-charter`>>

!! Room Charter

This parent keeps only branch-level signal framing:

* the exchange-boundary contract for `lar` URI signal
* the split between the `aim` / `yield` bearing vectors, the sigil panel, and in-span OODA-HA surfacing
* routing pressure toward the correct child room

Long witness bundles, migration residue, drift-recovery detail, symbol tables, and research argument should leave this parent.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-lar-signal`>>

!! The Lar Signal

This doc covers the `lar` URI signal layer:

* Agent-Operator exchange-boundary instrumentation
* the `aim` / `yield` bearing vectors that open and close a turn
* the relation between the `lar:` bearing vector, the sigil panel (`hud` · `ward`, the `syad` / `mu` lenses), and adjacent protocol surfaces

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/lararium-contract`>>

!! Lararium Contract

The lararium sigil panel does not merely decorate output based on lar URIs.
It closes the loop at exchange boundaries and makes the node's commitments legible.

The Agent-Operator contract reads:

* the `aim` reads operator intent before response
* the `aim` declares the role the node adopts before turn generation
* OODA-HA phase markers surface during generation, banded by the gauge
* `Aperture` / `OODA-HA` banded visibility rather than all-or-nothing disclosure

This loci explains why that loop matters on the lararium side.
Detailed emit rules and protocol-wide render contracts still live outward.

<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/lar-uri`>>

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/intent-headers`>>

!! Exchange Boundary Contract

Every substantive exchange opens with an `aim` vector, rides the `hud` · `ward` panel, then enters the governed span and closes on `yield`.

> ''Canonical URI Rule:'' every `lar:` URI in the exchange stream stays canonical ASCII record form — no emoji, no non-ASCII. Glyphs belong to the sigil panel and render surfaces, never the address. This keeps every emitted URI directly ingestible by MemPalace, crystal logs, and registry tools.

The frame runs as follows:

# Read operator intent as a provisional bearing vector.
  Lares reads the operator's prompt as an implicit signal: semantic bearing (HA.KA.BA) and the role it implies.
  The `~` prefix may mark the HA.KA.BA when the reading stays uncertain.

# Open the turn with the `aim` vector — operator intent `->` the role the node adopts.

```
<<~ set lares=`aim` from=`lar:///operator.intent.reads` to=`lar:///lares.role.acts`>>
```
  The `~` prefix marks an execution-provisional heading — a declared aim, not a confirmed landed resource.

# Ride the panel beneath the `aim`.
  ``<<~ set lares=`aim` aperture=`N/<band>` ooda-ha=`N/<band>`>>`` · `drift-ward="<the pull this island carries>"`, plus the `syad` / `mu` lenses when summoned. No band, number or marker rides beside a claim: the sentence names its own ground (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/mu/l-prime#/warrant`).

# Generate, then close.
  OODA-HA phase markers MAY surface forward inline, banded by the gauge.
  The turn closes on ``<<~ set lares=`yield` from=`lar:///lares.what.landed` to=`?`>>``.

Detailed panel anatomy lives in the HUD room.
Annotation thresholds and OODA-HA surfacing examples live in sibling signal rooms.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/layer-split`>>

!! Layer Split

The signal branch splits across five layers:

| Layer | What it carries | Primary room |
|---|---|---|
| Canonical URI vector | audit-ready record form for exchange boundaries | parent branch framing, see `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/docs/signal/l-space` |
| Sigil panel | live exchange-boundary instruments (`hud` · `ward`, the `syad` / `mu` lenses) | `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/docs/signal/hud` |
| Conformance lens | reads the OODA-HA loop in //referenced// content, outward and on demand | `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/conformance` |
| Render targets | cross-surface sigilization and projection rules | `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/docs/signal/render-targets` |
| SA-display framing | shared-mental-model theory, research grounding, and SA/XAI split | `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/docs/signal/sa-display` |

The `aim` vector governs prospectively.
The OODA-HA surfacing annotates the loop inside that governed span.
The render layer projects the same signal differently across surfaces without rewriting the underlying contract.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/parent-boundaries`>>

!! Parent Boundaries

Text that clearly belongs outward:

* sigil panel field tables and exchange-boundary instrument reading → `signal/hud.md`
* drift-recovery protocol pressure → `signal/drift.md`
* provenance, witness strands, and snapshot residue → `signal/provenance.md`
* shared-situation-awareness research framing and SA-vs-XAI argument → `signal/sa-display.md`
* l-space slot definitions and address semantics → `signal/l-space.md`
* render-surface mapping tables and per-surface conventions → `signal/render-targets.md`

The current chronometer material still reads as a research cluster under `signal/chronometer/`, not a settled room.

